  "body": "My apologies if this is explained somewhere, but after an hour of googling turned up no good answers I had to come here...\r\n\r\nThis will pre-populate the date input as expected:\r\n```\r\n<input type=\"date\" value=\"2023-02-09\">\r\n```\r\nThis does not:\r\n```\r\n<input type=\"date\" value=\"2023-02-09T22:00:00.000Z\">\r\n```\r\nBoth are valid ISO strings. I was totally expecting the time portion to be ignored and the date shown.\r\n\r\nI'm hoping someone can point me to the reasoning behind this.",
